{"term":"hand","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:b172b6265858fa2bb2","definition":"The part of the forelimb below the forearm or wrist in humans and other primates, and the corresponding part in many other animals.","example":"Her hands are really strong.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["manus","mound","mund","paw"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["handle"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hand#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e0f33aa84d48c80c3a","definition":"That which resembles, or to some extent performs the office of, a human hand.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["biscuit hooks","hand","mauler","meat hook"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["handle"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hand#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e90100fad2f395486a","definition":"That which is, or may be, held in a hand at once.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["biscuit hooks","hand","mauler","meat hook"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["handle"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hand#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d1a2c857e0039fdb14","definition":"In linear measurement:","example":"Boxer was an enormous beast, nearly eighteen hands high, and as strong as any two ordinary horses put together.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["biscuit hooks","hand","mauler","meat hook"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["handle"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hand#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"k